# Git and GitHub CLI Rules

## GitHub CLI (gh) Commands

This repository has multiple remotes (`origin` and `upstream`) because it's a fork structure.
When using `gh` commands, always specify the `--repo` option to avoid ambiguity.

### Creating Pull Requests

```bash
# Good: Always specify --repo
gh pr create --repo bufferings/eslint-plugin-neverthrow --base main --head branch-name --title "title" --body "body"

# Bad: May fail due to multiple remotes
gh pr create --base main --head branch-name --title "title" --body "body"
```

## Release Management

This project uses **changesets** for release management.

### Commands

- `pnpm changeset` - Create a new changeset
- `pnpm version-packages` - Update versions based on changesets
- `pnpm release` - Publish to npm

### Beta/Prerelease

```bash
# Enter beta mode
pnpm changeset pre enter beta

# Exit beta mode
pnpm changeset pre exit
```

When in beta mode, versions will be like `0.2.13-beta.0`.
